+
+### Phase evidence contract (new captures)
+
+`phaseSchema: 1` on collector receipts requires bounded `phases` summaries on every collection/persistence observation. Each fixed operation has count, total wall/thread CPU, failure count and actual maximum start/end/thread CPU/failure. Nested names (for example manifest publication and its fsync) overlap; their totals must never be added. No per-file paths or values enter phase labels. `phases.validate_capture` checks current-version records; old captures retain their frozen readers and unknown internal phases.
+
+Each collection window owns completed source/stat/read/prefix, archive validation/write/flush/fsync and manifest publication/flush/fsync operations. Cooperative checkpoint service closes a window only between leaf operations; there is no spanning checkpoint phase. Counts/maximums reflect only that window. The existing previousIntervalPersistence and lastIntervalPersistence carry poll serialization/write/flush/fsync after it completes, including failure. Its error propagates and guards still include actual persistence cost.
+
+Runtime heartbeats occur outside collection. A completed heartbeat observation carries actual start/end, run/clock and precedingPollStart (null plus startup=true for the initial heartbeat). Contiguous heartbeat sequence/count binds complete carrier coverage. The next collection row consumes previousHeartbeat once; the receipt carries only a still-unconsumed lastHeartbeat. The heartbeat file never claims its own future fsync. Startup manifest/collector initialization and final receipt/final heartbeat durability are not phase measured; no endpoint is invented for those writes. After emergency child reaping, the wrapper can reread an actual collector receipt bound to schema/run/clock/owned identity; its own signal/failure outcome stays authoritative. If a failure prevents the existing evidence write, telemetry can be incomplete, never a successful certificate.
+
+Overlap expands heartbeat and persistence carriers uniquely, rejecting repeated complete pairs and duplicate heartbeat identities. Only containing operation intervals enter overlap; nested phase summaries do not inflate it or alter target samples. Current rehearsal verification and independent native proof require strict phase validation before acceptance.
+
+There are19 fixed names, at most19 summaries per observation, and a16KiB phase-summary validation bound. Runtime memory is one fixed-name recorder per active window plus completed carriers, independent of archive history. No new durable file or fsync is added. Phase bookkeeping, JSON serialization and extra bytes remain inside the existing actual time guards. Observer overhead is measured in preparation; this is observability, not a remedy for historical latency or evidence of long-run reliability.
